IMPORT prelude

-- Undesirable Publications Act 1967 (Singapore) -- what counts as a publication and as supply (s 2), obscene and objectionable
-- (ss 3, 4), the offences and penalties for prohibited publications (ss 6, 7), forfeiture (s 9), the offences for obscene and
-- objectionable publications (ss 11, 12), return of seized items (s 13(3)), searches without warrant (s 10(2)), declarations at the
-- border (s 16), corporate officers (s 17), detention, destruction and appeal (ss 15, 16, 20), and exemptions (s 21).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation, version in force from 9/3/2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/UPA1967.txt. The latest amendment
-- annotated is Act 5 of 2025 (wef 09/03/2025), to s 18 (appointment of controllers).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0055 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The Act is short, so almost all of it is here. Not encoded: the Minister's power to make a
-- prohibition order (s 5) beyond its effect, the s 4(2) list of matters a controller must consider, package examination (s 8),
-- Magistrate's warrants (ss 10(1), 13(1)), the court's disposal order (s 13(2)), arrest (s 14), the bar to legal proceedings
-- (s 19), the appointment of controllers (s 18), and any prohibition order or regulation (none was retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Undesirable Publications Act 1967 -- publications`

§§ `2 -- publication and supply`

-- s 2: "publication" means any of the following "other than a film": (a) any book, magazine or periodical, "whether in manuscript
-- or final form"; (b) any sound recording; (c) any picture or drawing, "whether made by computer graphics or otherwise"; (d) any
-- photograph or negative; (e) any paper, tape, disc, article or thing with words or signs on it, or on which information is stored
-- that a computer can reproduce as a picture, word or sign; "and includes a copy of any publication".
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `a printed book`
    `a handwritten manuscript`
    `a music CD`
    `a computer-generated drawing`
    `a photographic negative`
    `a USB stick holding image files`
    `a cinema film`

GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is a publication` IF
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `a cinema film` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 2: "supply" includes (a) supply "by means of the electronic transmission of the contents"; (b) "hire, exchange or loan".
-- "electronic transmission" includes "facsimile transmission, electronic mail" but "excludes broadcasting".
-- INFERENCE: the definition of supply is inclusive ("includes"), so the text does not say broadcasting can never be supply; it says
-- only that broadcasting is not electronic transmission. The encoding treats broadcasting as falling outside supply.
DECLARE Mode IS ONE OF
    `handing over a copy`
    `lending a copy`
    `hiring out a copy`
    `exchanging a copy`
    `emailing the contents`
    `faxing the contents`
    `broadcasting the contents`

GIVEN `the mode` IS A Mode
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mode is supply` IF
    CONSIDER `the mode`
    WHEN `broadcasting the contents` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3, 4 -- obscene and objectionable`

-- s 3: a publication is obscene if its effect "or ... the effect of any one of its parts or items is, if taken as a whole, such as
-- to tend to deprave and corrupt persons who are likely ... to read, see or hear" it.
GIVEN `the whole tends to deprave and corrupt` IS A BOOLEAN, `any one distinct part tends to deprave and corrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication is obscene` IF
    `the whole tends to deprave and corrupt` OR `any one distinct part tends to deprave and corrupt`

-- s 4(1): objectionable "if, IN THE OPINION OF ANY CONTROLLER, it or ... any one of its parts or items" deals with (a) "matters
-- such as sex, horror, crime, cruelty, violence or the consumption of drugs" so that its availability "is likely to be injurious to
-- the public good"; or (b) "matters of race or religion" so that it "is likely to cause feelings of enmity, hatred, ill will or
-- hostility between different racial or religious groups". s 4(3): the question is "a matter for the expert judgment" of the person
-- deciding, and evidence "is not essential to its determination".
GIVEN `a controller thinks it injurious to the public good` IS A BOOLEAN, `a controller thinks it likely to cause racial or religious enmity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication is objectionable` IF
    `a controller thinks it injurious to the public good` OR `a controller thinks it likely to cause racial or religious enmity`

§ `Undesirable Publications Act 1967 -- offences`

§§ `6 -- prohibited publications`

-- s 6(1): any person who "imports, publishes, sells, offers for sale, supplies, offers to supply, exhibits, distributes or
-- reproduces any prohibited publication or any extract therefrom" -- first offence: fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to
-- 3 years or both; "for a subsequent offence to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 4 years".
-- s 6(2): "without reasonable excuse has in his possession" a prohibited publication or extract -- first offence: fine up to $2,000
-- or imprisonment up to 12 months or both; subsequent offence: imprisonment up to 2 years.
-- s 6(3): on a possession charge the accused "shall be presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have known the contents".
-- A "prohibited publication" is one whose importation, sale or circulation the Minister has prohibited by Gazette order (s 5).
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `importing`
    `publishing`
    `selling`
    `offering for sale`
    `supplying`
    `offering to supply`
    `exhibiting`
    `distributing`
    `reproducing`
    `possessing`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `the publication or extract is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is a section 6 offence` IF
        `the publication or extract is prohibited`
    AND CONSIDER `the dealing`
        WHEN `possessing` THEN NOT `has a reasonable excuse`
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- No fine is provided for a subsequent offence under s 6(1) or (2); the encoding returns 0 for "no fine provided".
GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `is a subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 6 maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `is a subsequent offence` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the dealing`
         WHEN `possessing` THEN 2000
         OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `is a subsequent offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 6 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `possessing` THEN (IF `is a subsequent offence` THEN 24 ELSE 12)
    OTHERWISE (IF `is a subsequent offence` THEN 48 ELSE 36)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `knowledge of the contents is presumed` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `possessing` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `7 -- delivery to a police station`

-- s 7(1): a person (a) to whom a prohibited publication "is sent without his knowledge or privity or is sent in response to a request
-- made by that person before the prohibition ... came into effect"; or (b) who has it "in his possession at the time when the
-- prohibition ... comes into effect", shall "forthwith" deliver it to the officer in charge of a police station. (2): failure -- fine
-- up to $1,000 or imprisonment up to 12 months or both.
DECLARE Receipt IS ONE OF
    `sent unsolicited`
    `ordered before the prohibition`
    `already held when the prohibition took effect`
    `ordered after the prohibition`

GIVEN `the receipt` IS A Receipt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must deliver it to a police station` IF
    CONSIDER `the receipt`
    WHEN `ordered after the prohibition` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the receipt` IS A Receipt, `delivered it to a police station` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to deliver is an offence` IF
    `must deliver it to a police station` `the receipt` AND (NOT `delivered it to a police station`)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 7 maximum fine` MEANS 1000

§§ `9 -- forfeiture`

-- s 9: a court "if satisfied that any document produced in the proceedings is a prohibited publication ... shall, whether the alleged
-- offender is convicted or not, order such publication ... to be forfeited to the Commissioner of Police".
GIVEN `the court is satisfied it is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN, `the accused is convicted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court must order forfeiture` IF
    `the court is satisfied it is prohibited`

§§ `11, 12 -- obscene and objectionable publications`

-- s 11 (obscene) and s 12 (objectionable), each "not being a prohibited publication": any person who (a) "makes or reproduces, or
-- makes or reproduces for the purposes of sale, supply, exhibition or distribution to any other person"; (b) "imports or has in his
-- possession for the purposes of sale, supply, exhibition or distribution to any other person"; or (c) "sells, offers for sale,
-- supplies, offers to supply, exhibits or distributes to any other person", "knowing or having reasonable cause to believe" it to be
-- obscene (objectionable). s 11: fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or both. s 12: fine up to $5,000 or imprisonment up
-- to 12 months or both. No higher penalty for a subsequent offence.
-- Limb (a) begins "makes or reproduces" with no purpose attached; the encoding reads it literally, so making for oneself is caught.
-- Limb (b) needs a purpose of passing it on, so importing or keeping one for oneself is not.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `making it for own use`
    `making it to sell`
    `copying it for own use`
    `importing it for own use`
    `importing it to sell`
    `keeping it for own use`
    `keeping it to distribute`
    `selling it`
    `giving it to a friend`
    `showing it to others`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is caught by sections 11 and 12` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `importing it for own use` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `keeping it for own use` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `it is obscene` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or had reasonable cause to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a section 11 offence` IF
        `the conduct is caught by sections 11 and 12` `the conduct`
    AND `it is obscene`
    AND (NOT `it is prohibited`)
    AND `knew or had reasonable cause to believe`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct, `it is objectionable` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is prohibited` IS A BOOLEAN, `knew or had reasonable cause to believe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is a section 12 offence` IF
        `the conduct is caught by sections 11 and 12` `the conduct`
    AND `it is objectionable`
    AND (NOT `it is prohibited`)
    AND `knew or had reasonable cause to believe`

DECLARE Kind IS ONE OF
    `obscene`
    `objectionable`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 11 or 12 maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `obscene` THEN 10000
    WHEN `objectionable` THEN 5000

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 11 or 12 maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `obscene` THEN 24
    WHEN `objectionable` THEN 12

§§ `16 -- declarations at the border`

-- s 16(1): any importer and any person entering Singapore shall, "if he is required to do so by a controller or any authorised
-- officer", declare whether he has any publication and produce it. (4): failure -- (a) person entering Singapore, fine up to $1,000;
-- (b) importer, fine up to $5,000. No imprisonment is provided.
DECLARE Arrival IS ONE OF
    `a person entering Singapore`
    `an importer`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Arrival, `was required by a controller or authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `declared and produced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to declare is an offence` IF
    `was required by a controller or authorised officer` AND (NOT `declared and produced`)

GIVEN `who` IS AN Arrival
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the section 16 maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a person entering Singapore` THEN 1000
    WHEN `an importer` THEN 5000

§§ `17 -- officers of companies and associations`

-- s 17(1): where an offence by a body corporate "is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be
-- attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer", the officer as well as the body corporate is guilty. (4), (5): the same
-- for partners and for officers or governing-body members of unincorporated associations.
GIVEN `the organisation committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `neglect is attributable to the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the organisation committed an offence` AND (`consented` OR `connived` OR `neglect is attributable to the officer`)

§ `Undesirable Publications Act 1967 -- seizure, detention and appeal`

§§ `10(2) -- search without warrant`

-- s 10(2): a police officer "not below the rank of sergeant" with reasonable cause to believe a prohibited publication is concealed in
-- any place, and "good grounds for believing that, by reason of the delay in obtaining a search warrant, the object of the search is
-- likely to be frustrated", may enter and search as if under a warrant.
DECLARE Rank IS ONE OF
    `constable`
    `corporal`
    `sergeant`
    `inspector`

GIVEN `the rank` IS A Rank
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rank is sergeant or above` IF
    CONSIDER `the rank`
    WHEN `constable` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `corporal` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the rank` IS A Rank, `has reasonable cause to believe` IS A BOOLEAN, `delay would frustrate the search` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may search without a warrant` IF
    `the rank is sergeant or above` `the rank` AND `has reasonable cause to believe` AND `delay would frustrate the search`

§§ `13(3) -- return of seized obscene or objectionable publications`

-- s 13(3): where (a) in proceedings under s 11 or 12 "no order is made" for disposal, or (b) "no such proceedings are instituted
-- within 3 months of the seizure", the publication or equipment "shall be returned" to the person from whom it was seized (or, if
-- that is not reasonably practicable, disposed of as lost or unclaimed property).
GIVEN `months since seizure` IS A NUMBER, `proceedings were instituted` IS A BOOLEAN, `proceedings ended without a disposal order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the seized item must be returned` IF
        `proceedings ended without a disposal order`
    OR  ((NOT `proceedings were instituted`) AND `months since seizure` GREATER THAN 3)

§§ `15, 16, 20 -- detention, destruction and appeal`

-- s 15(2)(b), s 16(3): where no proceedings are instituted within 3 months of the detention, the controller "may return" the article,
-- or "if the publication is obscene or objectionable or returning the article is not reasonably practicable", may "subject to
-- section 20" destroy it (s 16(3) also allows an order to export it).
-- s 20(5): no article "shall be destroyed under section 15 or 16 unless its detention has not been appealed against or an appeal
-- against its detention has been dismissed or abandoned".
DECLARE Appeal IS ONE OF
    `no appeal`
    `appeal pending`
    `appeal dismissed`
    `appeal abandoned`
    `appeal allowed`

GIVEN `the appeal` IS AN Appeal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal does not bar destruction` IF
    CONSIDER `the appeal`
    WHEN `no appeal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `appeal dismissed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `appeal abandoned` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `months since detention` IS A NUMBER, `proceedings were instituted` IS A BOOLEAN, `believed obscene or objectionable` IS A BOOLEAN, `return is not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the appeal` IS AN Appeal
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the controller may destroy it` IF
        (NOT `proceedings were instituted`)
    AND `months since detention` GREATER THAN 3
    AND (`believed obscene or objectionable` OR `return is not reasonably practicable`)
    AND `the appeal does not bar destruction` `the appeal`

-- s 20(1): a person aggrieved by detention under s 15 or 16 may appeal to the Minister, "whose decision shall be final". (2): no appeal
-- unless "notice of appeal in writing together with the reasons" is given "within 14 days of the date of service" of the notification.
-- (4): a posted notification is served on "the day on which [it] would be received in the ordinary course of post".
GIVEN `days after service` IS A NUMBER, `in writing with reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is allowed to proceed` IF
    `in writing with reasons` AND `days after service` AT MOST 14

§§ `21 -- exemptions`

-- s 21(3): the Minister, "if satisfied that the publication should be made available to a limited class of persons or to a particular
-- person for educational, professional, scientific, artistic or technical reasons", may exempt that class or person, for a period and
-- (4) absolutely or on conditions. (2): application on the Chief Controller's form with the prescribed fee.
DECLARE Reason IS ONE OF
    `educational`
    `professional`
    `scientific`
    `artistic`
    `technical`
    `personal enjoyment`
    `selling to the general public`

GIVEN `the reason` IS A Reason
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reason can support an exemption` IF
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `personal enjoyment` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `selling to the general public` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
